# Controller Patterns and REST API Design

## Overview
Controllers handle HTTP requests and responses, following REST principles and standardized response patterns. They delegate business logic to services and use DTOs for data transfer.

## Controller Structure

### 1. Basic Controller Pattern
```java
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/v1/timesheets")
@Validated
public class TimesheetController implements ITimesheetController {
    
    private final ITimesheetService timesheetService;
    private final APIResponder apiResponder;
    private final Logger logger;
    
    public TimesheetController(ITimesheetService timesheetService,
                              APIResponder apiResponder,
                              Logger logger) {
        this.timesheetService = timesheetService;
        this.apiResponder = apiResponder;
        this.logger = logger;
    }
}
```

### 2. Interface-First Design
```java
public interface ITimesheetController {
    ResponseEntity<?> createTimesheet(@Valid @RequestBody TimesheetRequestDto request);
    ResponseEntity<?> getTimesheetById(@PathVariable Integer id);
    ResponseEntity<?> updateTimesheet(@PathVariable Integer id, @Valid @RequestBody TimesheetRequestDto request);
    ResponseEntity<?> deleteTimesheet(@PathVariable Integer id);
    ResponseEntity<?> getTimesheetsByCandidate(@PathVariable Integer candidateId);
    ResponseEntity<?> bulkCreateTimesheets(@Valid @RequestBody BulkTimesheetRequestDto request);
}
```

## HTTP Method Patterns

### 1. POST - Create Operations
```java
@PostMapping
public ResponseEntity<?> createTimesheet(@Valid @RequestBody TimesheetRequestDto request) {
    try {
        logger.logInfo("Creating timesheet for candidate: " + request.candidateId());
        
        TimesheetResponseDto result = timesheetService.createTimesheet(request);
        
        return apiResponder.respond(result, "Timesheet created successfully");
        
    } catch (ValidationErrorException ex) {
        logger.logWarn("Validation error creating timesheet: " + ex.getMessage());
        return apiResponder.respondWithError(ex.getMessage(), HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);
        
    } catch (UnauthorizedAccessException ex) {
        logger.logWarn("Permission denied creating timesheet: " + ex.getMessage());
        return apiResponder.respondWithError(ex.getMessage(), HttpStatus.FORBIDDEN);
        
    } catch (Exception ex) {
        logger.logError("Unexpected error creating timesheet", ex);
        return apiResponder.respondWithError("Failed to create timesheet", HttpStatus.INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR);
    }
}
```

### 2. GET - Read Operations
```java
@GetMapping("/{id}")
public ResponseEntity<?> getTimesheetById(@PathVariable Integer id) {
    try {
        logger.logInfo("Fetching timesheet with id: " + id);
        
        TimesheetResponseDto result = timesheetService.getTimesheetById(id);
        
        return apiResponder.respond(result, "Timesheet retrieved successfully");
        
    } catch (ResourceNotFoundException ex) {
        logger.logWarn("Timesheet not found with id: " + id);
        return apiResponder.respondWithError(ex.getMessage(), HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND);
        
    } catch (UnauthorizedAccessException ex) {
        logger.logWarn("Permission denied accessing timesheet: " + ex.getMessage());
        return apiResponder.respondWithError(ex.getMessage(), HttpStatus.FORBIDDEN);
        
    } catch (Exception ex) {
        logger.logError("Unexpected error fetching timesheet", ex);
        return apiResponder.respondWithError("Failed to retrieve timesheet", HttpStatus.INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR);
    }
}
```

### 3. PUT - Update Operations
```java
@PutMapping("/{id}")
public ResponseEntity<?> updateTimesheet(@PathVariable Integer id, 
                                        @Valid @RequestBody TimesheetRequestDto request) {
    try {
        logger.logInfo("Updating timesheet with id: " + id);
        
        TimesheetResponseDto result = timesheetService.updateTimesheet(id, request);
        
        return apiResponder.respond(result, "Timesheet updated successfully");
        
    } catch (ResourceNotFoundException ex) {
        logger.logWarn("Timesheet not found for update with id: " + id);
        return apiResponder.respondWithError(ex.getMessage(), HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND);
        
    } catch (ValidationErrorException ex) {
        logger.logWarn("Validation error updating timesheet: " + ex.getMessage());
        return apiResponder.respondWithError(ex.getMessage(), HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);
        
    } catch (Exception ex) {
        logger.logError("Unexpected error updating timesheet", ex);
        return apiResponder.respondWithError("Failed to update timesheet", HttpStatus.INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR);
    }
}
```

### 4. DELETE - Delete Operations
```java
@DeleteMapping("/{id}")
public ResponseEntity<?> deleteTimesheet(@PathVariable Integer id) {
    try {
        logger.logInfo("Deleting timesheet with id: " + id);
        
        timesheetService.deleteTimesheet(id);
        
        return apiResponder.respond(null, "Timesheet deleted successfully");
        
    } catch (ResourceNotFoundException ex) {
        logger.logWarn("Timesheet not found for deletion with id: " + id);
        return apiResponder.respondWithError(ex.getMessage(), HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND);
        
    } catch (UnauthorizedAccessException ex) {
        logger.logWarn("Permission denied deleting timesheet: " + ex.getMessage());
        return apiResponder.respondWithError(ex.getMessage(), HttpStatus.FORBIDDEN);
        
    } catch (Exception ex) {
        logger.logError("Unexpected error deleting timesheet", ex);
        return apiResponder.respondWithError("Failed to delete timesheet", HttpStatus.INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR);
    }
}
```

## Bulk Operations

### 1. Bulk Create Controller
```java
@PostMapping("/bulk")
public ResponseEntity<?> bulkCreateTimesheets(@Valid @RequestBody BulkTimesheetRequestDto request) {
    try {
        logger.logInfo("Bulk creating " + request.timesheets().size() + " timesheets");
        
        BulkTimesheetResponseDto result = timesheetService.bulkCreateTimesheets(request);
        
        String message = String.format("Bulk operation completed. Success: %d, Errors: %d", 
            result.successful().size(), result.errors().size());
        
        return apiResponder.respond(result, message);
        
    } catch (ValidationErrorException ex) {
        logger.logWarn("Validation error in bulk timesheet creation: " + ex.getMessage());
        return apiResponder.respondWithError(ex.getMessage(), HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);
        
    } catch (Exception ex) {
        logger.logError("Unexpected error in bulk timesheet creation", ex);
        return apiResponder.respondWithError("Failed to process bulk timesheet creation", 
            HttpStatus.INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR);
    }
}
```

### 2. Bulk Permission Check Controller
```java
@PostMapping("/bulk-permission-check")
public ResponseEntity<?> bulkPermissionCheck(@Valid @RequestBody BulkPermissionCheckRequest request) {
    try {
        logger.logInfo("Performing bulk permission check for " + request.getItems().size() + " items");
        
        BulkPermissionCheckResult result = bulkPermissionChecker.checkBulkPermissions(request);
        
        return apiResponder.respond(result, "Bulk permission check completed");
        
    } catch (ValidationErrorException ex) {
        logger.logWarn("Validation error in bulk permission check: " + ex.getMessage());
        return apiResponder.respondWithError(ex.getMessage(), HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);
        
    } catch (Exception ex) {
        logger.logError("Unexpected error in bulk permission check", ex);
        return apiResponder.respondWithError("Failed to perform bulk permission check", 
            HttpStatus.INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR);
    }
}
```

## Search and Pagination

### 1. Search Controller
```java
@GetMapping("/search")
public ResponseEntity<?> searchTimesheets(@Valid SearchRequestBodyDto searchRequest,
                                         @Valid PaginationRequestBodyDto pagination) {
    try {
        logger.logInfo("Searching timesheets with criteria: " + searchRequest.toString());
        
        PaginatedResponseDto<TimesheetResponseDto> result = timesheetService.searchTimesheets(
            searchRequest, pagination);
        
        return apiResponder.respond(result, "Timesheet search completed");
        
    } catch (ValidationErrorException ex) {
        logger.logWarn("Validation error in timesheet search: " + ex.getMessage());
        return apiResponder.respondWithError(ex.getMessage(), HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);
        
    } catch (Exception ex) {
        logger.logError("Unexpected error in timesheet search", ex);
        return apiResponder.respondWithError("Failed to search timesheets", HttpStatus.INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR);
    }
}
```

### 2. Filtered List Controller
```java
@GetMapping("/candidate/{candidateId}")
public ResponseEntity<?> getTimesheetsByCandidate(@PathVariable Integer candidateId,
                                                 @RequestParam(defaultValue = "1") Integer page,
                                                 @RequestParam(defaultValue = "20") Integer size) {
    try {
        logger.logInfo("Fetching timesheets for candidate: " + candidateId);
        
        PaginationRequestBodyDto pagination = new PaginationRequestBodyDto(page, size, "createdAt", "DESC");
        List<TimesheetResponseDto> result = timesheetService.getTimesheetsByCandidate(candidateId, pagination);
        
        return apiResponder.respond(result, "Timesheets retrieved successfully");
        
    } catch (ResourceNotFoundException ex) {
        logger.logWarn("Candidate not found: " + candidateId);
        return apiResponder.respondWithError(ex.getMessage(), HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND);
        
    } catch (Exception ex) {
        logger.logError("Unexpected error fetching timesheets for candidate", ex);
        return apiResponder.respondWithError("Failed to retrieve timesheets", HttpStatus.INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR);
    }
}
```

## Response Handling

### 1. Standardized Response Pattern
```java
@RestController
public class BaseController {
    
    protected ResponseEntity<?> handleSuccess(Object data, String message) {
        return apiResponder.respond(data, message);
    }
    
    protected ResponseEntity<?> handleError(String message, HttpStatus status) {
        return apiResponder.respondWithError(message, status);
    }
    
    protected ResponseEntity<?> handleValidationError(String message) {
        return apiResponder.respondWithError(message, HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);
    }
    
    protected ResponseEntity<?> handleNotFound(String message) {
        return apiResponder.respondWithError(message, HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND);
    }
    
    protected ResponseEntity<?> handleUnauthorized(String message) {
        return apiResponder.respondWithError(message, HttpStatus.FORBIDDEN);
    }
}
```

