## Validation and Error Handling

### 1. Input Validation
```java
@PostMapping
public ResponseEntity<?> createTimesheet(@Valid @RequestBody TimesheetRequestDto request,
                                        BindingResult bindingResult) {
    if (bindingResult.hasErrors()) {
        List<ValidationErrorDto> errors = bindingResult.getFieldErrors().stream()
            .map(error -> new ValidationErrorDto(
                error.getField(),
                error.getDefaultMessage(),
                error.getRejectedValue()))
            .toList();
        
        return apiResponder.respondWithValidationErrors(errors);
    }
    
    // Process request
    return processCreateRequest(request);
}
```

### 2. Global Exception Handling
```java
@RestControllerAdvice
public class GlobalExceptionHandler {
    
    @ExceptionHandler(ValidationErrorException.class)
    public ResponseEntity<?> handleValidationError(ValidationErrorException ex) {
        return apiResponder.respondWithError(ex.getMessage(), HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);
    }
    
    @ExceptionHandler(ResourceNotFoundException.class)
    public ResponseEntity<?> handleResourceNotFound(ResourceNotFoundException ex) {
        return apiResponder.respondWithError(ex.getMessage(), HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND);
    }
    
    @ExceptionHandler(UnauthorizedAccessException.class)
    public ResponseEntity<?> handleUnauthorized(UnauthorizedAccessException ex) {
        return apiResponder.respondWithError(ex.getMessage(), HttpStatus.FORBIDDEN);
    }
    
    @ExceptionHandler(Exception.class)
    public ResponseEntity<?> handleGenericException(Exception ex) {
        return apiResponder.respondWithError("An unexpected error occurred", 
            HttpStatus.INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR);
    }
}
```

## Access Control Integration

### 1. Permission-Based Controller
```java
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/v1/timesheets")
public class TimesheetController {
    
    @GetMapping("/{id}")
    public ResponseEntity<?> getTimesheetById(@PathVariable Integer id) {
        // Check permission using bulk permission checker
        BulkPermissionCheckRequest permissionRequest = BulkPermissionCheckRequest.builder()
            .items(List.of(BulkPermissionCheckRequest.BulkPermissionCheckItem.builder()
                .entity(Entity.TIMESHEET)
                .permissionCheckContext(PermissionCheckContext.builder()
                    .permission(Permission.VIEW_TIMESHEET)
                    .permissionLevel(PermissionLevel.YES)
                    .build())
                .accessControlCheckMetadataContext(AccessControlCheckMetadataContext.builder()
                    .timesheetId(id)
                    .build())
                .build()))
            .build();
        
        BulkPermissionCheckResult permissionResult = bulkPermissionChecker.checkBulkPermissions(permissionRequest);
        
        if (!permissionResult.getResults().get(0).isAllowed()) {
            return apiResponder.respondWithError("Access denied", HttpStatus.FORBIDDEN);
        }
        
        // Process request
        return processGetRequest(id);
    }
}
```

## Best Practices

### 1. Controller Design
- Keep controllers thin - delegate business logic to services
- Use consistent error handling patterns
- Implement proper logging for debugging
- Use appropriate HTTP status codes

### 2. Request/Response Handling
- Use DTOs for all input/output
- Validate input at controller level
- Use standardized response formats
- Handle exceptions gracefully

### 3. Performance
- Use pagination for large result sets
- Implement caching where appropriate
- Use async operations for long-running tasks
- Monitor response times

### 4. Security
- Implement proper authentication/authorization
- Validate all input parameters
- Use HTTPS in production
- Log security-related events

### 5. Documentation
- Use OpenAPI annotations for API documentation
- Provide clear error messages
- Document response formats
- Include usage examples



